@node Overview
@chapter Overview

Spofy is a full-featured Spotify client that runs entirely inside Emacs.  It communicates with the @uref{https://developer.spotify.com/documentation/web-api, Spotify Web API} to provide playback control, search, browsing, playlist management, and library management without leaving the editor.

The package targets Emacs 30 or later and depends on the @samp{transient} library (available on GNU ELPA) for its command popup.  Optional integrations are provided for @samp{consult} (minibuffer completion), @samp{embark} (contextual actions), and @samp{org-mode} (link storage and export).

Spofy is organized as a multi-file package.  The main entry point is the @samp{spofy} command, which opens a dashboard buffer showing the current track, recently played tracks, and the user's playlists.  From there, the user can search for content, browse albums and artists, manage playlists, and control playback.  A transient popup (@ref{Transient popup}) provides quick access to all commands from any buffer.

The core capabilities are:

@itemize
@item
@strong{Authentication:} OAuth2 authorization code flow with a local HTTP callback server and persistent encrypted token storage (@ref{Authentication}).
@item
@strong{Playback control:} Play, pause, skip, seek, adjust volume, toggle shuffle and repeat.  Timer-based polling keeps the UI in sync with the player state (@ref{Playback control}).
@item
@strong{Search:} Dedicated commands for searching tracks, albums, artists, and playlists, each displaying results in a @code{tabulated-list} buffer (@ref{Search}).
@item
@strong{Browsing:} Detail views for albums, artists, and playlists with contextual keybindings (@ref{Browsing}).
@item
@strong{Playlist management:} Full CRUD operations on playlists: create, rename, delete, add, remove, and reorder tracks (@ref{Playlist management}).
@item
@strong{Library management:} View and manage saved tracks and albums (@ref{Library management}).
@item
@strong{Mode-line display:} A configurable mode-line segment showing the currently playing track (@ref{Mode-line display}).
@item
@strong{Tab-bar display:} A configurable tab-bar segment showing the currently playing track (@ref{Tab-bar display}).
@end itemize

