@node Getting started
@section Getting started

Before using Spofy, you must register a Spotify application:

@enumerate
@item
Go to the @uref{https://developer.spotify.com/dashboard, Spotify Developer Dashboard} and create a new application.
@item
In the application settings, add @samp{http://127.0.0.1:8080/spofy/callback} as a redirect URI (adjust the port if you change @code{spofy-redirect-port}).
@item
Note the Client ID and Client Secret.
@end enumerate

Then configure Spofy in your init file:

@lisp
(setq spofy-client-id "your-client-id")
(setq spofy-client-secret "your-client-secret")
@end lisp

Run @samp{M-x spofy-authenticate} to authorize Spofy with your Spotify account.  This opens your browser to the Spotify authorization page.  After granting access, the browser redirects to the local server and Spofy stores the tokens in @code{spofy-token-file} (defaults to @samp{spofy-tokens.gpg} in the user Emacs directory, encrypted via EasyPG).  Subsequent sessions reuse the stored tokens automatically.

Once authenticated, run @samp{M-x spofy} to open the dashboard.

