@node Authentication (1)
@section Authentication

@vindex spofy-client-id
@vindex spofy-client-secret
@vindex spofy-redirect-port
@vindex spofy-token-file

The user option @code{spofy-client-id} holds the Client ID of your registered Spotify application.  It defaults to @code{nil}.  Without this value, Spofy cannot communicate with the Spotify API@.  Obtain it from the Spotify Developer Dashboard (@ref{Getting started}).

The user option @code{spofy-client-secret} holds the Client Secret of your registered Spotify application.  It defaults to @code{nil}.  Like the client ID, this is required for the OAuth2 token exchange.

The user option @code{spofy-redirect-port} controls the port on which Spofy's temporary OAuth2 callback server listens.  It defaults to @code{8080}.  Change this if port 8080 is already in use on your machine.  The redirect URI registered in the Spotify Developer Dashboard must match the port you configure here.

The user option @code{spofy-token-file} specifies where Spofy stores OAuth tokens.  It defaults to @samp{spofy-tokens.gpg} in the user Emacs directory.  The @samp{.gpg} extension causes Emacs to encrypt the file via EasyPG; use a plain @samp{.el} extension to store tokens unencrypted.

@node Playback
@section Playback

@vindex spofy-poll-interval
@vindex spofy-seek-seconds
@vindex spofy-volume-step
@vindex spofy-no-device-action

The user option @code{spofy-poll-interval} sets the number of seconds between player state polls.  It defaults to @code{5}.  Lower values make the UI more responsive to changes (e.g. track transitions) at the cost of more API requests.  The Spotify API does not provide push notifications, so polling is the only way to detect state changes.

The user option @code{spofy-seek-seconds} controls how many seconds @code{spofy-seek-forward} and @code{spofy-seek-backward} jump.  It defaults to @code{10}.

The user option @code{spofy-volume-step} sets the percentage increment for @code{spofy-volume-up} and @code{spofy-volume-down}.  It defaults to @code{5}.  Valid volume values range from 0 to 100.

The user option @code{spofy-no-device-action} determines what happens when Spofy tries to control playback but no active Spotify device is found.  It defaults to the symbol @code{prompt}, which displays a message asking the user to open Spotify on any device.  Setting it to @code{launch} makes Spofy attempt to start the local Spotify desktop application automatically (using @samp{open -a Spotify} on macOS or @samp{spotify} on Linux).

@node Mode-line
@section Mode-line

@vindex spofy-mode-line-format
@vindex spofy-mode-line-max-length
@vindex spofy-mode-line-separator

The user option @code{spofy-mode-line-format} is a format string that controls what the mode-line segment displays.  It defaults to @code{"▶ %t — %a"}.  The following specifiers are available:

@multitable {aaaaaaaaa} {aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa}
@headitem Specifier
@tab Meaning
@item @samp{%t}
@tab Track name
@item @samp{%a}
@tab Artist name
@item @samp{%b}
@tab Album name
@item @samp{%p}
@tab Play/pause icon (▶ or ⏸)
@item @samp{%s}
@tab Shuffle indicator (⇌ when on, empty when off)
@item @samp{%r}
@tab Repeat indicator (↻ for context, ↻₁ for track, empty)
@end multitable

The user option @code{spofy-mode-line-max-length} sets the maximum character length of the mode-line string.  It defaults to @code{40}.  Longer strings are silently truncated.  Increase this if you have a wide frame and want to see more of the track and artist names.

The user option @code{spofy-mode-line-separator} is the string inserted before the Spofy segment in the mode line.  It defaults to a single space.

@node Tab-bar
@section Tab-bar

@vindex spofy-tab-bar-format
@vindex spofy-tab-bar-max-length

The user option @code{spofy-tab-bar-format} is a format string that controls what the tab-bar segment displays.  It defaults to @code{"%p %t — %a"}.  The same format specifiers as @code{spofy-mode-line-format} are supported (@ref{Mode-line}).

The user option @code{spofy-tab-bar-max-length} sets the maximum character length of the tab-bar string.  It defaults to @code{50}.  Longer strings are silently truncated.  Set it to @code{nil} to disable truncation entirely.

@node Global key and mode-line activation
@section Global key and mode-line activation

@vindex spofy-global-key
@vindex spofy-enable-mode-line
@vindex spofy-enable-tab-bar

The user option @code{spofy-global-key} sets the prefix key that @code{spofy-global-mode} binds to @code{spofy-menu}.  It defaults to @code{"C-c s"}.  Change this if the default conflicts with other bindings.

The user option @code{spofy-enable-mode-line} controls whether @code{spofy-global-mode} automatically enables @code{spofy-mode-line-mode}.  It defaults to @code{t}.  Set it to @code{nil} if you prefer a clean mode line and want to access now-playing information only through the dashboard or transient popup.

The user option @code{spofy-enable-tab-bar} controls whether @code{spofy-global-mode} automatically enables @code{spofy-tab-bar-mode}.  It defaults to @code{nil}.  Set it to @code{t} to display the currently playing track in the tab bar (@ref{Tab-bar display}).

