@node Authentication
@section Authentication

@findex spofy-authenticate

The command @code{spofy-authenticate} initiates the Spotify OAuth2 authorization flow.  It starts a temporary HTTP server on @code{spofy-redirect-port}, opens the user's default browser to Spotify's authorization page, and waits for the redirect callback.  Once the user grants access, Spofy exchanges the authorization code for access and refresh tokens, stores them in @code{spofy-token-file}, and shuts down the temporary server.

After successful authentication, Spofy runs @code{spofy-authenticated-hook}.  You only need to authenticate once; subsequent sessions reuse the stored refresh token to obtain new access tokens automatically.

@node Dashboard and global control
@section Dashboard and global control

@findex spofy
@findex spofy-dashboard-refresh
@findex spofy-stop

The command @code{spofy} is the main entry point.  It ensures that the user is authenticated (prompting if not), starts player state polling, and opens the @samp{*Spofy*} dashboard buffer.  The dashboard displays three sections:

@enumerate
@item
@strong{Now playing:} the current track name, artist, album, a text progress bar, and playback state indicators (play/pause, shuffle, repeat).
@item
@strong{Recently played:} the last 10 tracks, each a clickable button that replays the track.
@item
@strong{Your playlists:} the user's first 10 playlists, each a clickable button that opens the playlist detail view.  A ``View all playlists@dots{}'' link at the bottom opens the full playlists list.
@end enumerate

The now-playing section refreshes automatically when the player state changes.  The command @code{spofy-dashboard-refresh} forces a full refresh of the entire dashboard.

The command @code{spofy-stop} stops player state polling and disables @code{spofy-global-mode}.  Use it when you are done with Spofy and want to stop all background activity.

The dashboard keymap provides these bindings:

@multitable {aaa} {aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa}
@headitem Key
@tab Command
@item @samp{p}
@tab @code{spofy-play-pause}
@item @samp{n}
@tab @code{spofy-next}
@item @samp{b}
@tab @code{spofy-previous}
@end multitable
@samp{/}  | @code{spofy-menu}           |
@multitable {aaa} {aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa}
@item @samp{g}
@tab @code{spofy-dashboard-refresh}
@item @samp{q}
@tab @code{quit-window}
@end multitable

@node Transient popup
@section Transient popup

@findex spofy-menu

The command @code{spofy-menu} opens a transient popup that provides quick access to all Spofy commands from any buffer.  The popup header shows the currently playing track.  When @code{spofy-global-mode} is active, this command is bound to @code{spofy-global-key} (default @samp{C-c s}).

The popup is organized into three columns:

@itemize
@item
@strong{Playback:} play/pause, next, previous, seek forward, seek backward.
@item
@strong{Browse:} search tracks/albums/artists/playlists, library, playlists list, device selection.
@item
@strong{Volume, Mode & Other:} volume controls (volume up/down keep the menu open), shuffle/repeat toggles, dashboard, quit.
@end itemize

A sub-transient for the library (@ref{Library management}) is available from the browse column.

@node Global minor mode
@section Global minor mode

@findex spofy-global-mode

The command @code{spofy-global-mode} toggles a global minor mode.  When enabled, it:

@itemize
@item
Binds @code{spofy-global-key} to @code{spofy-menu}.
@item
Starts player state polling.
@item
Enables the mode-line display (if @code{spofy-enable-mode-line} is non-nil).
@end itemize

When disabled, it reverses all of these effects.  The @code{spofy} command enables this mode automatically.

@node Playback control
@section Playback control

@findex spofy-play-pause
@findex spofy-next
@findex spofy-previous
@findex spofy-seek-forward
@findex spofy-seek-backward
@findex spofy-volume-up
@findex spofy-volume-down
@findex spofy-volume-set
@findex spofy-toggle-shuffle
@findex spofy-toggle-repeat
@findex spofy-play-track
@findex spofy-play-context

The command @code{spofy-play-pause} toggles playback between playing and paused.  It checks the current state and sends the appropriate API call.

The commands @code{spofy-next} and @code{spofy-previous} skip to the next or previous track, respectively.

The commands @code{spofy-seek-forward} and @code{spofy-seek-backward} move the playback position by @code{spofy-seek-seconds} seconds (@ref{Playback, , Playback options}).

The commands @code{spofy-volume-up} and @code{spofy-volume-down} adjust the volume by @code{spofy-volume-step} percent.  The command @code{spofy-volume-set} prompts for an exact volume level between 0 and 100.

The command @code{spofy-toggle-shuffle} toggles shuffle mode on or off.  The command @code{spofy-toggle-repeat} cycles through three repeat states: off, context (repeat the current album/playlist), and track (repeat the current track).

The command @code{spofy-play-track} plays a specific track by its Spotify URI@.  If an optional context URI is provided (an album or playlist URI), playback starts within that context at the specified track.  The command @code{spofy-play-context} plays an entire context (album, playlist, or artist) from the beginning.  Both commands are used internally by the browse and search interfaces.

@node Polling
@section Polling

@findex spofy-player-start-polling
@findex spofy-player-stop-polling

The command @code{spofy-player-start-polling} starts a timer that polls the Spotify player state at @code{spofy-poll-interval} second intervals.  Polling is necessary because the Spotify Web API does not support push notifications.  When the player state changes, Spofy runs @code{spofy-player-state-changed-hook}.  When the track changes specifically, it also runs @code{spofy-player-track-changed-hook}.  When the API reports no active player session (e.g. playback ended or the device went idle), Spofy clears the player state and runs @code{spofy-player-state-changed-hook} so that the mode line and tab bar reflect that nothing is playing.  Polling errors are caught unconditionally (even when @code{debug-on-error} is non-nil) to prevent them from stalling the repeat timer.

The command @code{spofy-player-stop-polling} cancels the polling timer.  Polling is started automatically by the @code{spofy} command and @code{spofy-global-mode}, and stopped by @code{spofy-stop}.

@node Device management
@section Device management

@findex spofy-select-device

The Spotify Web API can control playback on any device logged into the user's account: desktop apps, mobile phones, web players, smart speakers, and more.  The command @code{spofy-select-device} fetches the list of available devices, presents them in a @code{completing-read} prompt, and transfers playback to the selected device.

When no active device is found, Spofy's behavior depends on @code{spofy-no-device-action} (@ref{Playback, , Playback options}).

@node Search
@section Search

@findex spofy-search-tracks
@findex spofy-search-albums
@findex spofy-search-artists
@findex spofy-search-playlists

Spofy provides four search commands, each targeting a specific entity type:

@itemize
@item
@code{spofy-search-tracks} searches for matching tracks.
@item
@code{spofy-search-albums} searches for matching albums.
@item
@code{spofy-search-artists} searches for matching artists.
@item
@code{spofy-search-playlists} searches for matching playlists.
@end itemize

When @code{spofy-consult} is loaded, these commands use incremental search via @code{consult--dynamic-collection}: the minibuffer appears immediately and candidates update live as you type.  Without @code{spofy-consult}, they fall back to prompting for a query string and displaying results in a tabulated list.

Each command creates a @samp{*Spofy Search: TYPE*} buffer using @code{tabulated-list-mode}.  The columns vary by entity type:

@multitable {aaaaaaaaa} {aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa}
@headitem Type
@tab Columns
@item Tracks
@tab Play indicator, Name, Artist(s), Album, Duration
@item Albums
@tab Name, Artist(s), Year, Tracks
@item Artists
@tab Name, Genres, Followers
@item Playlists
@tab Name, Owner, Tracks, Public
@end multitable

If the currently playing track appears in the search results, it is highlighted with the @code{spofy-playing} face and prefixed with a ▶ icon.

