The command @code{spofy-library-save} saves a Spotify entity (track or album) to the user's library.  It accepts a Spotify URI and determines the entity type from it.  The command @code{spofy-library-unsave} removes an entity from the library.  Both commands are available through keybindings in search, browse, and library buffers.

@node Cache management
@section Cache management

@findex spofy-clear-cache

Spofy caches API responses in memory to reduce network requests and improve responsiveness.  Each endpoint type has its own time-to-live: search results are cached for 5 minutes, user playlists for 1 minute, playlist tracks for 2 minutes, and album/artist details for 10 minutes.  The player state endpoint is never cached.

The command @code{spofy-clear-cache} flushes the entire in-memory cache.  Use it when you suspect stale data, for example after making changes to a playlist in the Spotify app.  The cache is also cleared automatically when Emacs restarts.

